# Project Handoff Maintenance

The `docs/project/` package is the single source of truth. Maintenance is
mandatory; significant work is not complete until the package is reviewed.

At session start, read `AI_HANDOFF.md`, `PROJECT_CONTEXT.json`, and
`NEXT_SESSION.md`; verify branch, working tree, PR, and release state.

Review/update the package after any feature add/remove/change, bug fix,
refactor, architecture/product decision, epic start/completion, phase
completion, release, merge, technical-debt change, dependency change, CI/CD
change, or significant documentation update.

Always review all eight files; modify only affected ones:
`AI_HANDOFF.md`, `PROJECT_STATE.md`, `ARCHITECTURE_STATE.md`,
`PRODUCT_STATE.md`, `DECISION_LOG.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `NEXT_SESSION.md`, and
`PROJECT_CONTEXT.json`.

Rules:

- Summarize outcomes; never paste commit logs.
- Keep executive state, phase/epic, version/release, branch, providers, risks,
  completed/in-progress work, roadmap, and next actions consistent.
- Product Decisions require ID, date, status, decision, rationale, and impact.
- Never delete decisions; record reversals as new entries.
- `NEXT_SESSION.md` must state objective, prerequisites, blockers, and
  acceptance criteria.
- Do not claim a PR merged, release published, or test passed without evidence.
- Keep `PROJECT_CONTEXT.json` valid JSON.
- Validate internal links plus version, branch, date, and JSON consistency.

Completion gate: code complete, tests passing, docs updated, handoff updated,
and validation complete. Only then mark the task complete.
